From 2fa4113ab9e13bea36657500a09a5b5935b513f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 07:44:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06852/11362] [outer-loop] ARC bp35 round-3: L4->L5, resolves
 round-2 safe-timing hypothesis

Round-3 codex gpt-5.6-sol attempt on bp35 solved L5: second gravity switch
clicked from center safe column (confirms the round-2 x=33 safe-timing
hypothesis was on the right track, though the exact mechanism is
column-position not just timing), two open-X toggle blocks solidified into
a protective ceiling, 3x2 E barrier tunnel entered from lower-right with
only the lower row removed.

Independently verified: 5x fresh env.reset() + replay via resolve_replay_plan
(new >=5 priority branch, dict-normalized labels), all 5 trials confirmed
level=5, state=GameState.NOT_FINISHED.

reproducible_total_levels 143 -> 144. arc_count_integrity_lint.py exit 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
